WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:07.534
This is Anthropic, Read Aloud. Today: Building an A I-native revenue organization.

2
00:00:08.834 --> 00:00:11.611
Building an A I-native revenue organization.

3
00:00:12.061 --> 00:00:24.133
In this guide, Anthropic shares how revenue leaders can roll out Claude across a sales organization, including the setup decisions, a three-phase rollout plan, and an R O I measurement framework.

4
00:00:24.583 --> 00:00:28.711
From Claude Blog, published September 15, 2026.

5
00:00:29.711 --> 00:00:52.353
In our conversations with revenue leaders, we hear the same challenges: half the team barely touches the A I it already has, the best sellers build skills and prompts that no one else uses, and leadership has no visibility into usage and spend. Meanwhile, sellers gather account context before every call from multiple systems: the CRM, email, call recordings, Slack.

6
00:00:52.473 --> 00:00:56.632
That can mean spending thirty minutes on prep for fifteen minutes of conversation.

7
00:00:57.082 --> 00:01:17.156
Individual reps can save time every day when they hand over call prep to Claude, but when the whole team adopts it, the benefits compound. How much a sales organization gets out of Claude depends on what it has built around it: which systems Claude can read and write and whether it has the access and controls to take on more complex work.

8
00:01:17.606 --> 00:01:32.432
Cox Communications reported a 7 x return in its first-year of A I investment and cut the cost of validating and enriching sales leads by 86 percent, bringing accuracy up from 18 percent to 97 percent.

9
00:01:32.552 --> 00:01:47.238
At Cyera, where 88 percent of roughly 1500 employees use Claude weekly, BDRs draft outreach with a skill that’s been built using the top performers’ best work, a quality improvement as much as a time saving.

10
00:01:47.688 --> 00:01:56.796
To help revenue teams get the most out of A I, we put together Building an A I-native revenue organization, a guide to rolling out Claude across sales.

11
00:01:57.246 --> 00:01:58.350
In the guide, we share:

12
00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:04.414
A maturity model showing where your organization stands today and what it takes to reach the next level.

13
00:02:04.654 --> 00:02:12.600
The setup decisions to make before the pilot: owners, connectors, IT and security, success metrics, and spend visibility.

14
00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:19.665
A three-phase rollout plan (set up, pilot, scale) with the use cases revenue teams run most, mapped by role.

15
00:02:19.905 --> 00:02:25.303
How to measure R O I in three groups: efficiency, expansion, and new capabilities.

16
00:02:25.543 --> 00:02:29.790
The pitfalls that stall org-wide rollouts, and checklists for getting started.

17
00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:31.305
Read the guide here.

18
